From e5f585ebc8f7eeac87ffc879bb97cc63ce3a1687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Pelka <tpelka@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:31:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] afc: Avoid double free when service_receive() fails

When service_receive() returns an error and reports zero bytes received,
the error branch frees dump_here but does not return, so the following
zero-bytes branch frees it again. Return the error right after freeing.

This also covers the partial-read-with-error case, where the short-read
branch would free the same buffer a second time.

Signed-off-by: Tomas Pelka <tpelka@redhat.com>
Resolves: RHEL-291675
---
 src/afc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/afc.c b/src/afc.c
index dfc33ec..2b33a51 100644
--- a/src/afc.c
+++ b/src/afc.c
@@ -328,6 +328,7 @@ static afc_error_t afc_receive_data(afc_client_t client, char **bytes, uint32_t
 		if (err != AFC_E_SUCCESS) {
 			free(dump_here);
 			debug_info("Failed to receive data: %s (%d)", afc_strerror(err), err);
+			return err;
 		}
 		if (*bytes_recv <= 0) {
 			free(dump_here);
-- 
